body_en:
The fight against unwanted isolation in Álava has made significant progress with the approval of the first grant call for municipalities and local administrative divisions. This initiative, part of the *Araba a Punto* strategy, was approved by the Foral Social Welfare Body (GOFE) and will fund nine projects across eight municipalities. The grants aim to equip local governments with resources to design programs and activities that foster interpersonal connections, prevent loneliness, and enhance social cohesion in their communities.

A total of €50,000 will support initiatives in Urkabustaiz, Iruraiz-Gauna, Berantevilla, Artziniega, Laguardia, Agurain, Amurrio, and Donemiliaga. These projects will implement targeted measures to prevent, identify, and address unwanted loneliness, including community support programs, intergenerational activities, and the revival of collective memory. They will also establish volunteer networks, training for detecting isolation cases, and dedicated spaces for social interaction—particularly for older adults and other vulnerable groups.

As part of the *Araba a Punto* strategy, the grants seek to strengthen community care networks and empower local entities to develop tailored initiatives. Among the selected projects, Iruraiz-Gauna’s care program will implement a comprehensive community plan for preventing, detecting, and responding to loneliness. Artziniega’s *Artziniega konektatzen: Komunitatea eta Zaintza* project will focus on building community networks and fostering intergenerational connections.

Donemiliaga’s *Nagusi Biziak* initiative will provide meeting and prevention activities for residents, while Amurrio will pilot a project exploring the creation of rural spaces for social interaction. Other key initiatives include:
- **Urkabustaiz**, using cultural activities to strengthen rural social bonds;
- **Berantevilla**, reviving collective memory to foster community cohesion;
- **Laguardia**, launching two programs to improve the well-being and social engagement of older adults;
- **Agurain**, developing a community-focused approach to prevent and address loneliness.
